## Problem Statement

Small grocery stores in villages still use physical *"Vahi"* books to track customer credit. When these books get damaged or lost, it causes:
- Financial loss and disputes between shopkeeper and customer
- No automated balance calculation (manual errors)
- No reminder system for pending dues
- No daily business summary

---

## Solution

Grama Khata provides:
- Simple Give/Take interface (Koduvudu / Tegedukolluvudu)
- Offline-first storage using Room Database
- Real-time net balance calculation per customer
- AI-generated daily collection reports via Google Gemini
- One-tap WhatsApp payment reminders

---

## Features

| Feature | Description |
|---|---|
| Customer Management | Add/delete customers with name, phone, and initials avatar |
| Transaction Logging | Simple + (PAID) and − (DUE) buttons for credit/debit |
| Real-time Balance | Net balance updates instantly after every transaction |
| Due Dashboard | All customers sorted by highest amount owed |
| AI Daily Report | Gemini AI generates a daily collection summary |
| WhatsApp Reminder | AI-generated polite reminder sent via WhatsApp |
| Offline First | All core features work fully without internet |

---

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology | Version |
|---|---|---|
| Language | Kotlin | 2.0.0 |
| Architecture | MVVM | — |
| Local Database | Room DB | 2.6.1 |
| State Management | LiveData + ViewModel | 2.7.0 |
| AI Feature | Google Gemini 1.5 Flash API | Latest |
| HTTP Client | Retrofit | 2.9.0 |
| Async | Kotlin Coroutines | 1.7.3 |
| UI | Material Components | 1.11.0 |
| Navigation | Jetpack Navigation Component | 2.7.6 |
| WhatsApp | Intent.ACTION_VIEW | — |

---

## Architecture

```
UI Layer (Fragments + Activities)
        ↕
ViewModel Layer (Business Logic)
        ↕
Repository Layer (Data Management)
        ↕
Room DB (Local) + Gemini AI API (Cloud)
```

